{
	"version": 1,
	"_comment": "The camp, the bags and repair. Every number is a PLACEHOLDER to tune by feel. Gold is the one currency (always available). 'materials' are stackable resources (monsters drop them, repairs and upgrades use them); a stack of up to 'stack' of one material takes one bag slot. The RUN BAG is what a player carries into a stage (loot goes in at once, and it is lost if the player dies); the STASH is the permanent store at camp. Repair: restoring a worn item costs gold and a little ore per point (normal); an item that has worn down to 0 costs much more and needs several kinds of material (broken). Both are multiplied by tier_multiplier for the item's tier (low tier first) and reduced by the workbench's repair_discount. Camp: raising the camp level unlocks facilities and camp skills; a facility is built and upgraded level by level (each level has a cost and may need a camp level) and its levels add effects: stash_slots, bag_slots, repair_discount; 'function' names what the camp screen lets the player do there (repair, enhance, farm...). start_levels are what a new player already has.",
